-- `Paint WITHAL` takes every field's TYPICALLY default and writes none
-- (TYPICALLY-ONE-BEHAVIOUR-SPEC.md T1). WITHAL is a keyword like WITH, and the
-- Check phase below must still have tokens for this file: the checker adds one
-- argument per field, none of which the author wrote.

DECLARE Colour IS ONE OF Red, Green

DECLARE Paint
  HAS colour IS A Colour TYPICALLY Red
      coats  IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 2

GIVETH A Paint
`stock` MEANS Paint WITHAL

#EVAL `stock`
